                <pb facs="0328" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg208"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-07-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                    1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Rockhill reports that the foreign office has informed him that the
                    provincial authorities have been strongly urged to restrain the boycott
                    movement, that a very strong stand against this movement has been taken by the
                    viceroy of this province, and that the authorities at Shanghai and elsewhere are
                    opposing the agitators.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
